  "description": "NANVOR crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C62 H86 Dy7 N17 O35 2+,2(Cl1 1-),3(C2 H3 N1),10(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy2A (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3A (Dy) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.550-3.910 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 93.70-114.97°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C66H113Cl2Dy7N20O45. Article name explicitly identifies I(I).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
